WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.849
A professional executive partnership makes work clear and commitments

00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:08.192
reliable In this unit you will translate priorities into

00:00:08.231 --> 00:00:13.205
support deliverables prepare a usable working agreement distinguish role

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:17.534
boundaries present options when demands conflict and arrange a

00:00:17.586 --> 00:00:21.718
concern route and sustainable cover Your two main work

00:00:21.784 --> 00:00:24.902
products are a working agreement and a priority decision

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:30.599
brief The Meridian people and arrangements are fictional Numerical

00:00:30.626 --> 00:00:35.613
examples are case facts not operating standards The course

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:39.889
does not grant workplace authority You will follow Daniel

00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:43.757
as he supports Lindiwe at Meridian Start with the

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:47.692
facts available at 07:40 make your own first brief

00:00:48.099 --> 00:00:51.981
and only then compare the later confirmed record Use

00:00:52.034 --> 00:00:55.060
the glossary for unfamiliar words and the source reading

00:00:55.086 --> 00:00:59.573
for detail Practice activities help you learn without adding

00:00:59.613 --> 00:01:03.376
to your formal mark The separate formative test lets

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:06.297
you try the agreed question and quiz retry rules

00:01:07.218 --> 00:01:10.060
Keep your practical portfolio as a draft for later

00:01:10.073 --> 00:01:13.994
feedback You can pause or replay narration and read

00:01:14.047 --> 00:01:18.152
the same material as text Use only fictional or

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.889
sanitised information in your responses
